text:
The app writes both `drift.token` and `drift.session.v1` when a session is claimed via the UI. In my spec, I'm seeding only `drift.session.v1` (REST claim + localStorage injection) — so `drift.token` doesn't exist. The app's restore works from the session object, but my teleport helper is reading `drift.token`.

Fix: within the teleport helper, either read the session object and extract the token, or inject `drift.token` too. The cleanest way: make the teleport helper read the token from the session object:

```ts
const token = await page.evaluate(() => {
  const t = localStorage.getItem('drift.token');
  if (t) return t;
  const raw = localStorage.getItem('drift.session.v1');
  try {
    return raw ? (JSON.parse(raw) as { token?: string }).token ?? null : null;
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
});
```

Even simpler: since the spec already has the session object `s` in scope, just pass the token directly: `async function teleport(page, baseURL, token, to)`. This is cleaner — planet-approach does exactly this (`teleport(page, baseURL, s.token, ...)`).

